<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror / Suspense</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Normal, but if someone can tell me how SCP-5999 was made, I might be able to do something like that.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> If you look at a picture of Dwarf Planet Ceres, you'll see a mysterious group of lights in the Occator Crater. I created an SCP based on the lights on Ceres.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Station Tau is an international research base located in the asteroid belt that is dedicated to multiple scientific pursuits, but mainly SCP-XXXX. Station Tau and Ceres were brought to the Foundation's attention after satellites reported after SCP-XXXX, a hot liquid substance was found being ejected from the Occator Crater on Ceres at a high altitude, almost like a volcano erupting. The Foundation then made a deal with officials from Station Tau that the Foundation would cooperate with all of Station Tau's initiatives, and in exchange, Station Tau would allow Foundation Personnel to investigate SCP-XXXX. SCP-XXXX will evaporate any non-planetary material, because of its high temperature. It can hijack all communications systems and broadcast visual and auditory signals that [DATA EXPUNGED] most who hear it. Those who were left unaffected recall seeing an organic lifeform burrowed at the core of Ceres or hearing a female voice speak about its disdain for life. It also creates clones of people who have been near SCP-XXXX (at a safe distance). The moment when SCP-XXXX hijacked Station Tau's communication systems is referred to as Comms Incident One. Shortly after Comms Incident One, a patrol station referred to as Occator-Alpha was placed, and personnel onboard the patrol station were tasked with collecting SCP-XXXX safely so it could be studied. However, when they attempted to extract SCP-XXXX, the station was destroyed and the comms went offline. The maximum height at which SCP-XXXX is being ejected from the surface of Ceres started rising the day Occator-Alpha was destroyed, and has been continually rising at an identical rate since. SCP-XXXX will eventually reach Earth in ██ years. As such, a contingency plan entitled Operation Theta was created in order to ensure the survival of Earth. The main element of the 'story' of SCP-XXXX is the use of the Station Tau Archive Database and Viewing System or STADaVS. It is used by various personnel to access files and either save or delete them.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The danger posed by SCP-XXXX and the element of suspense as you read down the article.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> If you want a draft, I can give the draft.</p>

